    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d731">

                <pb facs="0821" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg733"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr. McCormick.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-07-29"><hi rendition="#italic">July 29,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 134.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s telegram of
                    the 27th instant, relative to the seizure of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ardova</hi>, confirmed separately, I inclose for your information copies of
                    letters from the Acting Secretary of War and Henry W. Peabody &amp; Co.,<anchor
                        n="a" xml:id="d731-f1"/> relative to the military stores for the Philippine
                    government carried in that vessel.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis B. Loomis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d731-a1.xml" xpointer="d731-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
